      "title": "Arts Education Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Careers at St. Bonaventure University For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Arts Education Coordinator | Careers at St. Bonaventure University  page has loaded. Arts Education Coordinator | Careers at St. Bonaventure University  page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Careers at St. Bonaventure University powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Arts Education Coordinator Print Apply ﻿ Arts Education Coordinator Salary $18.00 Hourly Location St. Bonaventure, NY Job Type Part Time Job Number 202200632 Division Academic Affairs Department Quick Center for the Arts Opening Date 08/10/2026 Description Benefits Description The Regina A. Quick Center for the Arts seeks an energetic and creative individual to support arts education and engagement programming for K-12 students, St. Bonaventure University students, and community members. Applicants should have an interest in the fine arts, including visual art, music, theater, and dance, and a desire to help create meaningful arts experiences for diverse audiences. The individual will work with Quick Center staff to plan, coordinate, and support educational and public programs, including visual arts exhibitions, gallery tours, masterclasses in theater, music and dance, and community outreach initiatives. Examples of Duties Coordinate Fine Arts educational programs, tours, workshops, masterclasses, exhibitions, performances, and outreach activities. 20% Coordinate all aspects of three annual student art exhibitions featuring K-5, middle school, and high school students, including communication with participating schools and teachers, artwork intake, installation, exhibition logistics, and related events. 20% Collaborate with Curator and Executive Director on a Regional Arts Conference 10% Plan and implement community engagement activities 20% Maintain and organize educational materials, supplies, and program spaces. 10% Assist with exhibition installation, including painting and patching walls, preparing mats and frames, and hanging artwork and signage. 20% Typical Qualifications High school diploma Bachelor’s degree or college coursework or experience in visual arts, music, theater, dance, arts education, museum studies, art history, arts administration, or a related field preferred. 2 years of experience in arts education and community engagement. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Comfortable working with children, college students, and community members. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with staff, artists, educators, performers, faculty, and community partners. Knowledge of the fine arts, including visual arts, music, theater, and/or dance. Working Conditions / Physical Requirements Ability to Hang Artwork Ability to climb ladders Ability to lift 50lbs Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. St. Bonaventure University Perks Free access to campus fitness center Employee Assistance Program Golf course membership discount Other National and Local discounts available St. Bonaventure University is located in the scenic Enchanted Mountain region of Western New York, approximately 75 miles south of Buffalo, New York, with easy access to major metropolitan areas. A close-knit and caring community guided by its values of compassion, wisdom and integrity, St. Bonaventure is dedicated to academic excellence as informed by its Franciscan and liberal arts traditions. The university is committed to developing an inclusive community and preparing leaders dedicated to ethical conduct and compassionate service. The university currently enrolls approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and more than 1,000 graduate students in its schools of Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Communication, and Health Professions. U.S. News & World Report ranks SBU in the top 15% of regional universities in the North, for both value and overall. St. Bonaventure is a member of the Atlantic 10 Conference (NCAA Division I), with athletes participating in 20 sports. To view benefits offer to part-time SBU employees, click the link below: Part-Time Employee Benefits Employer St. Bonaventure University (NY) Address 3261 West State Road St. Bonaventure, New York, 14778 Website http://www.sbu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not ha